---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Assessment Disclaimer & Result Meaning | BDSM Test"
  description="Understand the limitations of the BDSM Test, the meaning of self-reported scores, and important consent and safety principles."
  canonicalPath="/disclaimer"
>
  <Header activePath="/disclaimer" />

  <main class="flex-1 py-12 md:py-20">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-16 h-80 hero-mesh"></div>

    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="mb-10">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-border bg-surface px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-mute shadow-xs">
          Transparency & Guidance
        </span>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-1.2px] text-ink">
          Assessment Disclaimer
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono text-mute">Please read carefully before taking or interpreting the assessment</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-xs space-y-8 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">1. Nature of Self-Assessment</h2>
          <p>
            The BDSM Test is a self-administered, educational tool designed to foster self-reflection, intimacy communication, and relationship dialogue.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your scores are based solely on your own subjective, self-reported answers at the moment of completion. Results should be viewed as an exploratory conversation starter rather than a definitive, immutable definition of who you are.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">2. Not a Medical or Psychological Instrument</h2>
          <p>
            This assessment is not a psychiatric diagnosis, clinical evaluation, or psychological measurement tool. It does not screen for, diagnose, or treat any mental health conditions, personality disorders, or relationship dysfunction.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are experiencing emotional distress, trauma, relationship difficulties, or mental health challenges, please consult a qualified healthcare provider, licensed therapist, or sex-positive counselor.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">3. Fluidity of Desires & Boundaries</h2>
          <p>
            Human sexuality, trust, and intimacy preferences are dynamic and often change over time, across different partners, relationship stages, and emotional headspaces.
          </p>
          <p>
            A high score in a specific dimension (such as Masochist, Submissive, or Primal Hunter) indicates an interest or curiosity—it does not mean you are required to act on it, nor does it imply consent to any scenario.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">4. Consent Is Mandatory and Revocable</h2>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-raised p-4 space-y-2 text-xs">
            <div class="font-semibold text-ink">Fundamental Rule of Kink:</div>
            <p>
              Consent can never be assumed, demanded, or enforced by test results. Consent must be ongoing, voluntary, enthusiastic, and can be withdrawn at any time, for any reason, with zero penalty.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="pt-2">
            Always establish unambiguous safewords before engaging in high-intensity activities, and practice dedicated aftercare to ensure physical and emotional well-being.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-border pt-6">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">5. Physical & Safety Risks</h2>
          <p>
            Certain forms of BDSM (including rope bondage, suspension, impact play, temperature play, and breath play) carry inherent physical hazards if practiced without proper anatomical education, ergonomic knowledge, and emergency release equipment.
          </p>
          <p class="text-xs text-mute">
            Users are solely responsible for their personal health, physical safety, and the well-being of their partners. BDSM Test assumes no responsibility or liability for any actions taken or scenes conducted by users.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

